# Previous and next navigation

Put both the direction and the destination title in each link, for example “Next: Restore from a backup”. On the first or last chapter, leave out the direction that does not exist.

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation. They do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use it for chapters in installation or recovery guidance. Use native date controls for Energy periods and native pagination for a results table. Those are not automatically the same pattern. See [Pagination](../../components/pagination.html) for results.

## Structure and behaviour

Give the navigation landmark its own name. Do not add an inert link where a direction is unavailable. Arrow artwork is optional, and the words must carry the meaning.

## Home Assistant boundary

Moving between guide pages must not submit a form or issue a device command. The examples use section anchors to show ordering inside one isolated page. A multi-page guide needs durable URLs and a consistent chapter list.

